o headquarters. Qualifications and Experience ㆍ Education : Bachelor’s degree in Chemical, Environmental, Electrical, Mechanical Engineering, or a related field. ㆍ Experience : 3+ years handling hazardous materials in data centers, power/chemical plants, or large industrial facilities. ㆍ Legal Requirement : Must meet the requirements for appointment as a Hazardous Chemical Manager (Article 12 of the Chemical Control Act Enforcement Decree). ㆍ Certifications : Relevant Engineer or Industrial Engineer certificate (e.g., Hazardous Materials, Waste Management, Environmental Risk, Chemical Process). ㆍ Skills : Proactive hazard mitigation, strong understanding of environmental/safety regulations, English proficiency (Preferred), and ability to respond to 24/7 emergencies (e.g., outages). HSE Manager [부산 강서구] Responsibilities ㆍ Risk & Incident Management : Conduct comprehensive risk assessments, implement actionable mitigation strategies, lead incident investigations, and perform root cause analyses to prevent recurrence. ㆍ Compliance & Audits : Ensure strict adherence to KOSHA, ISO 45001, and internal safety policies. Support compliance audits, manage corrective actions, and maintain meticulous HSE documentation. ㆍ Safety Culture & Training : Develop, coordinate, and deliver HSE training programs. Establish clear standard operating procedures (SOPs) and checklists to cultivate a high level of safety awareness. ㆍ Stakeholder Collaboration : Partner directly with contractors, clients, and regulatory agencies to transparently communicate HSE issues and support overarching safety objectives. Qualifications and Experience ㆍ Education : Bachelor’s degree in Occupational Safety, Environmental Science, Engineering, or a related discipline. ㆍ Experience : Minimum 3+ years of direct HSE implementation experience in mission- critical environments (data centers, oil & gas, commercial ops, or power plants). ㆍ Certifications : - Required : Industrial Safety Engineer. - Preferred : Industrial Engineer Hazardous Material, NEBOSH, CSP, NFPA 70E, or similar electrical/mechanical safety credentials. ㆍ Knowledge & Skills : Strong understanding of KOSHA and ISO 45001 frameworks. Excellent computer skills for HSE reporting and management systems. ㆍ Language & Eligibility : TOEIC 900+ (or equivalent) with excellent English communication skills. Must be legally authorized to work and reside in Korea. (Note : This is a safety-sensitive position). ELV Manager [부산 강서구] Responsibilities ㆍ Infrastructure Operations : Lead operations and maintenance for high-availability systems including DCIM, BMS, ACS, CCTV, SCADA, Local Instruments, and HVAC controls. Standardize emergency and preventive maintenance workflows. ㆍ Project & Vendor Management : Control ELV project schedules, budgets, and quality. Review engineering designs and final handovers, and strictly supervise vendors against SLAs. ㆍ Compliance & Optimization : Ensure compliance with local codes (IEEE, IEC, KEC) and safety regulations. Drive green initiatives to optimize Power Usage Effectiveness (PUE) and reduce costs. ㆍ Leadership & Reporting : Supervise and coach technical staff, assign tasks, and report critical operational metrics and system issues to executive management. Qualifications and Experience ㆍ Education : Bachelor’s degree in Electrical Engineering or a related discipline (Preferred). ㆍ Experience : Minimum 10 years of experience managing computer-based control systems (DCS, PLC) and communication equipment in data centers, industrial plants, or critical power environments. ㆍ Leadership : 3+ years of team leadership or management experience (Preferred). ㆍ Certifications : - Required : Industrial Engineer Fire Protection (or higher). - Preferred : Professional Electrical License (or equivalent), Engineer certificates (Information Processing/Communication/Security), CCNA, CCNP. ㆍ Skills : Strong technical expertise in DCIM/PLC/DCS. Good English communication skills. Ability to respond swiftly