t modifications. ㆍEnsure compliance with health and safety regulations on site. ㆍMaintain project records, including meeting minutes, logs, and progress photos. Qualifications and Experience ㆍBachelor's degree in Mechanical Engineering, Project Management, or related field. ㆍ10 years of experience in design and construction management or a related role. ㆍStrong knowledge of construction processes, materials, and building codes. ㆍProficient in construction project management software. (e.g., AutoCAD, MS Project) ㆍExcellent organizational, problem-solving, and communication skills. ㆍAbility to read and interpret construction drawings and technical documents. ㆍFamiliar with budgeting, scheduling, and project tracking tools. ㆍTeam player with the ability to manage multiple tasks and meet deadlines. ㆍEnglish communication skill and Data Center project experience are preferred. Mechanical Manager (Operations) [부산 강서구] Responsibilities ㆍLead and manage the operation, maintenance, and continuous improvement of all mechanical systems in the data center to ensure high system uptime and operational reliability. ㆍManage critical infrastructure including cooling systems(CRAC, CRAH, Chillers, Cooling Towers, CHWP/CWP, Containment), HVAC & ventilation systems, fire protection systems(Gas-based, VESDA, Sprinklers), plumbing systems, and emergency generator systems. ㆍDevelop and implement preventive maintenance(PM), inspections, and statutory compliance checks. ㆍEstablish and manage SOP, MOP, and EOP procedures, and develop emergency response and recovery plans. ㆍManage mechanical-related projects including upgrades and new installations, controlling schedule, budget, quality, and risk. ㆍReview system design and technical suitability, and oversee commissioning, integrated system testing, and handover processes. ㆍManage contractors, service providers, and suppliers, monitor SLA performance, and optimize contract execution and cost efficiency. ㆍEnsure compliance with applicable codes, safety regulations, and internal standards, and support audits with corrective actions. ㆍDrive energy efficiency initiatives(e.g., PUE improvement) and implement cost reduction and optimization programs. ㆍAssign tasks, manage team performance, provide coaching, and foster collaboration. ㆍPrepare regular reports for senior management and respond to/manage critical operational incidents. Qualifications and Experience ㆍBachelor’s degree in Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a related field. ㆍMinimum 10 years of experience in operation, maintenance, construction, or project management of critical facilities. (e.g., data centers, power plants, industrial plants) ㆍMinimum 3 years of leadership or people management experience preferred. ㆍHands-on experience with mechanical systems such as cooling(chillers, CRAH, etc.), HVAC, piping systems, and diesel generators/rotating equipment. ㆍStrong troubleshooting, Root Cause Analysis(RCA) capability, and ability to diagnose and resolve complex mechanical issues. ㆍStrong analytical and data-driven decision-making skills. ㆍAbility to work under pressure during emergencies. (e.g., power outages, system failures) ㆍRelevant professional certifications(e.g., Professional Engineer, licenses) preferred. ㆍWorking proficiency in English. (written and verbal) preferred Mechanical Engineer [부산 강서구] Responsibilities ㆍCritical Infrastructure Operations : Operate and maintain cooling systems(CRAC, CRAH, Chillers, Cooling Towers, Pumps, Containment), HVAC & ventilation, fire protection(Gas, VESDA, Sprinklers), plumbing, and emergency diesel generators. (including fuel systems) ㆍProcedures & Incident Management : Develop and manage SOP/MOP/EOP, preventive maintenance(PM) plans, and emergency recovery procedures. Conduct root cause analysis(RCA) and respond to critical operational incidents. ㆍProject & Commissioning Management : Oversee mechanical upgrades and new installations(controlling schedule, budget, risk, and quality). Review system designs, manage integrated system testing, and validate site handovers. ㆍVendor & Efficiency Management : Supervise contractors and suppliers against SLAs, optimize contracts, ensure regulatory compliance, and drive PUE(Power Usage Effectiveness) improvement initiatives. ㆍLift Safety Management : Act as the Lift Safety Manager to ensure safe operations, execute scheduled/preventive maintenance, manage spare parts, and legally renew certificates through accredited inspections. Qualifications and Experience ㆍBachelor’s degree in Mechanical Engineering or a related field. ㆍ3+ years of experience in critical facilities. (data centers, power plants, industrial plants) Hands-on experience with cooling, HVAC, diesel generators, rotating equipment, and lift maintenance. ㆍMinimum 1 year of people management or leadership experience. (Preferred) ㆍMechanical Engineer / Industrial Engineer certificate(or related) AND Craftsman Elevator(or higher). ㆍStrong analytical, troubleshooting, and RCA capabilities. Working proficiency in written and verbal English. (Preferred) ㆍAbility to work under pressure and respond effectively during emergencies. (e.g., power outages, system failures) 전형절차 ※ 전형절차 및 일정은 당사 사정에 따라 변경될 수 있습니다. (The selection process and schedule may be subject to change at the company's discretion.) ※ 모집분야 별로 필요 시 영어 인터뷰가 진행됩니다. (An English interview will be conducted if necessary, depending on the recruitment category.) 제출서류 ㆍ영문/국문 이력서, 자기소개서 ※ 모든 제출서류는 PDF 또는 MS WORD 파일로 제출 바랍니다. ※ 이력서 및 관련 제출 서류는 국문과 영문을 모두 반드시 제출해 주시기 바랍니다. (Applicants are required to submit their resume and relevant documents in both Korean and English.) ※ 영문 이력서가 제출되지 않으면 서류 검토가 진행되지 않을 수도 있습니다. (Please note that if an English resume is not submitted, the document review process may not proceed.) 접수기간 및 방법 ㆍ접수기간 : 2026년 09월 13일까지 ㆍ접수방법 : 국/영문 이력서, 자기소개서 기재하여 사람인 온라인 입사지원 기타사항 ㆍ서류전형 합격자에 한하여 개별 연락 드립니다. ㆍ입사지원서 기재 내용의 착오 또는 누락으로 인하여 발생한 불이익은 본인에게 책임이 있으며, 허위사실 기재 및 허위증빙서 제출 시 채용확정 이후라고 채용