utomation) 경험 - Static Analysis Tool 사용 경험 - Jira, Azure DevOps, TestRail 등 Test Management Tool 사용 경험 - 전공은 무관하나 아래 전공을 우대합니다. 컴퓨터공학 / 소프트웨어공학 / 전기 전자공학 / 의료공학 / 제어공학 / 로봇공학 Technology & Business Strategy (Associate Manager –Manager Level) (서울) 담당업무 This role is a key member of the Business Development Team. You will understand Angel Robotics' core technologies, uncover customer problems and market opportunities that have not yet been fully defined, and shape them into next-generation products and new businesses. You will connect internal research and development outcomes with external insights from customers, clinical practice, markets, public policy, and partners. Your work will help determine what we should productize, why we should act now, and what evidence should guide investment and execution. This is not a move away from research into administrative work. It is an opportunity to extend deep technical expertise into product strategy and business decision-making, and to help turn strong technology into products customers choose and businesses that can scale. Working in the Business Development Team in close partnership with the CEO, you will collaborate with R&D, RA/QA, clinical, manufacturing, marketing, sales, and finance. We are looking for a strategic operator who can convert uncertainty into testable hypotheses and executable plans, drive critical decisions, and stay accountable through productization and commercialization. This is not a role that simply manages a predetermined roadmap. As a core member of the team, you will help define Angel Robotics' next products and growth opportunities. You will work across the full lifecycle of an opportunity, from technology assessment and product strategy to the business case, partnerships, and launch readiness, while growing as a technology, product, and business leader. We are not looking for someone to manage answers that have already been decided. We are looking for someone who can ask better questions at the intersection of technology and the market, and help design the future the company should pursue. 자격사항 Key Responsibilities This role integrates complex technology, product, and business considerations to improve decision quality and help carry selected strategic initiatives through execution. Enterprise Technology, Product, and Business Opportunity Identification Analyze internal technology assets and product roadmaps alongside unmet customer needs, changes in clinical and industrial environments, competitive technologies, and public policy. Translate the most promising opportunities into clear Opportunity Theses and assess them based on strategic fit, feasibility, expected value, and risk. Current Product Competitiveness and Product Lifecycle Strategy Assess current products from an enterprise perspective, including customer value, clinical utility, usability, quality, serviceability, pricing, cost, and profitability. Use voice-of-customer, clinical, sales, service, and quality data to identify feature improvements, software and firmware updates, options and accessories, next-generation models, and service opportunities. Work with relevant teams to define the business case and priorities for maintaining, improving, expanding, or replacing each product. New Product and New Business Planning Define the target user, unmet need, core use case, and value proposition, and translate them into product concepts and high-level requirements. Build a coherent product logic covering intended use, critical functions and performance, differentiation, claims, regulatory and clinical pathways, target cost, and the business model. Validate key assumptions through customer interviews, field observation, prototypes, proofs of concept, and pilots, and continuously refine the product and business direction. Integrated Technology Strategy Across Software, Firmware, and AI Evaluate how mechanics, actuators, sensors, controls, embedded software and firmware, applications, cloud, AI, and data work together as an integrated product system. With technical teams, clarify trade-offs in performance, safety, usability, cybersecurity, data, schedule, and cost. Without replacing engineering design authority, connect technical choices to customer value, product requirements, and business objectives. Business Case Development and Stage-Gate Decision Support Develop business cases that go beyond market size to address adoption barriers, purchasing dynamics, pricing, target cost, margin, investment requirements, regulatory and clinical pathways, launch conditions, and key risks. Define the assumptions, validation plans, deliverables, owners, and decision criteria for each stage, and prepare Gate Reviews. Based on the evidence, present clear options and recommendations to Go, Pivot, Hold, or Stop. Domestic and International Business Opportunities and Strategic Partnerships Assess market opportunities and product fit by country and customer segment, and design market-entry logic covering regulation, clinical evidence, localization, pricing, channels, and service requirements. Develop collaboration models for co-development, validation, licensing, and market entry with hospitals, research institutions, technology companies, manufacturers, suppliers, public-sector organizations, and domestic and international business partners. Establish product-market fit, the partner model, and launch readiness so sales and marketing teams can execute for revenue. Cross-Functional Execution and Strategic Initiative Ownership For selected strategic initiatives, define the Program Charter, integrated milestones, functional owners, key dependencies, risks, and operating cadence. Frame cross-functional issues through the lens of product value and business viability, and escalate matters requiring resolution to functional leaders or executives at the right time. Use government-sponsored R&D programs and external funding opportunities as strategic assets to accelerate technology, products, regulatory approval, clinical evidence, pilots, and market entry. CEO Strategic Decision Support and Enterprise Opportunity Prioritization Synthesize internal technology assets, customer and market intelligence, cross-functional perspectives, and key data so the CEO can make balanced decisions across technology, product, business, and investment priorities. Structure critical management issues into clear questions, options, expected benefits, key risks, and a recommended course of action. Translate the opportunities the company should pursue into Opportunity Theses and Business Cases, and recommend priorities based on strategic fit, feasibility, and expected value. When warranted, objectively challenge existing assumptions or direction and present evidence-based alternatives and trade- offs across technology, market, and financial considerations. Convert the CEO's final decisions into specific initiatives, owners, and key milestones, and monitor follow-through and results. Qualifications - Master's degree or higher in robotics, mechanical engineering, electrical or electronic engineering, control engineering, computer science or AI, biomedical engineering, biomechanics, industrial engineering, or a related field. - A master's degree with 3-5 years of relevant experience, or a PhD, in R&D, product development, technology planning, product management, or technology commercialization. - For PhD candidates with exceptional product development, industry- academic collaboration, technology transfer, or commercialization experience, the experience requirement may be considered flexibly. - Deep expertise in at least one of software, firmware, or AI, with the ability to understand the relationship among hardware, software, firmware, and AI in a robotic product from a systems perspective. - Ability to quickly understand technical papers, patents, experimental results, and development documentation, and clearly explain both technical limitations and their product and business implications. - Ability to translate customer problems and technical possibilities into product requirements, business hypotheses, validation plans, and executable initiatives. - Demonstrated ability to collaborate across functions and levels, drive decisions, and ensure effective follow-through. - Ability to prepare clear, logical executive documents in Korean, understand technical documentation in English, and communicate effectively with global partners. - Prior in-house experience supporting a CEO or executive leadership team on strategic priorities and decision-making. 우대사항 - Experience in wearable robotics, medical devices, Physical AI, human-robot interaction, mobility, or assistive technology. - Experience in software, firmware, or AI development, systems engineering, verification, or productization for safety-critical or regulated products. - Experience collaborating with medical device product lifecycle, clinical, RA/QA, usability engineering, risk management, cybersecurity, or regulatory approval teams. - Experience in new product or new business planning, business case development, pricing and revenue models, venture building, or technology commercialization. - Experience with domestic or international customer interviews, voice-of- customer programs, field trials, market entry, or global partnerships. - Experience translating outcomes from government-sponsored R&D into product roadmaps, regulatory approval, clinical evidence, pilots, or commercialization. 근무조건 - 근무형태 : 정규직 (수습기간 3개월) - 근무요일 : 주 5일 (월~금) - 급여 : 회사내규에 따름 - 근무지역 : [플래닛 서울] 서울시 광진구 구의동 546-4 테크노마트21 제 12층 1호 공통자격조건 - 남성인 경우 병역필 또는 면제자 - 해외여행에 결격사유가 없는 분 전형절차 ※ 서류 검토는 1~2주 정도 소요되며, 서류 합격자에 한하여 순차적으로 연락 드립니다. 제출서류 - 이력서(자기소개서 필수, 상세경력 포함), 자격증 증명서(우대사항 해당 시 제출) 접수기간 및 방법 - 접수기간 : 각 포지션별 채용시 마감 - 접수방법 : 사람인 온라인 입사지원 기타사항 - 신입 지원 시, 성적 증명서 필수 첨부 부탁 드립니다. - 입사지원 서류에 허위사실이 발견될 경우, 채용확정 이후라도 채용이 취소될 수 있습니다. - 전형 결과 정규직 전형 불합격자 중 필요 시, 후보자에게 동의를 받아 계약직 전형으로 검토될 수 있습니다.",
